@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}
<div class="container container-background mt-4">
    <h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>
    <p class="text-muted">Last updated: June 2026</p>
    <p>
        This page summarizes how the WolflineSquad website handles your data. The complete,
        legally binding data-protection notice is our
        <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Gdpr">GDPR / Datenschutzerklärung</a>.
    </p>

    <section>
        <h2>1. Data we store</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>An internal user ID and your SteamID, used to identify you when you are signed in.</li>
            <li>Permissions assigned to your account (e.g. administrator or moderation rights).</li>
            <li>Your answer(s) when you take part in a poll, including your ranking order for ranking polls and the time you took part. Poll responses are <strong>not anonymous</strong> — they are tied to your account and can be viewed by authorized staff.</li>
            <li>Rewards you earned for taking part in a poll (in-game currency), and whether they have been paid out in-game.</li>
            <li>Marketplace activity tied to your SteamID: items you list for sale or auction (the item, price, type, end time), bids you place, and the resulting trades. Trades use in-game points only &mdash; no real money is involved. These transactions are logged (item, price, time) and can be viewed by authorized staff.</li>
            <li>Webhook configurations set by authorized staff (a target URL and which event). When the event fires (e.g. a new market listing) we POST an item/price message to that URL such as a Discord channel &mdash; these messages contain no personal data.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            When signed in, you can view your own in-game Pointshop inventory and currency, and authorized
            staff (with the relevant permission) can view a player's inventory. The website reads this live
            from the game server's database &mdash; it does not store its own copy and does not share it with
            any third party. You can also unequip your own equipped items from this page, which updates the
            game database directly.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>2. Sign-in with Steam</h2>
        <p>
            You can sign in using Steam (OpenID). We only receive your SteamID from Steam &mdash;
            no password or other Steam account details.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>3. Cookies</h2>
        <p>This site uses only strictly necessary cookies. We do not use tracking, analytics, advertising, or third-party cookies.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Session cookie</strong> (<code>.AspNetCore.Session</code>): keeps your session
                alive while you browse; removed when the browser is closed or the session expires.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Login cookie</strong> (<code>WolflineLogin</code>): set only when you sign in
                with Steam, so you stay logged in across visits. It stores only your SteamID in a signed
                (tamper-proof) form and lasts 30 days.
            </li>
        </ul>
        <p>You can remove the login cookie at any time by logging out or clearing your browser cookies.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>4. Your rights &amp; contact</h2>
        <p>
            You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of your data. For any data-protection
            request, contact <a href="mailto:admin@dasmaffin.com">admin@dasmaffin.com</a>.
        </p>
    </section>
</div>
